  "executive_briefing": "The crypto market ecosystem is defined by an impending September 15 legislative showdown over the Digital Asset Market CLARITY Act in the U.S. Senate. This bipartisan bill aims to formalize statutory boundaries between SEC and CFTC oversight while providing legal safety for advanced smart contract architectures. Simultaneously, Bitcoin spot ETF allocations have reached a maturity ceiling marked by structural plateauing and net outflows in early 2026, shifting focus toward treasury management and prime custody. In parallel, regulatory clarity is unlocking native Bitcoin programmability to directly compete with EVM dominance, while trust-minimized, non-custodial cross-chain routers (like LiFi and Symbiosis) rapidly displace traditional hack-prone bridges to unify BTC and ETH liquidity.",
